            <main class="col-lg-8">
                <p class="lead-copy">Foreign exchange and investment regulations require careful planning, accurate reporting and timely approvals. Sonagra &amp; Company assists businesses, promoters, investors and international groups with FEMA and FDI-related matters across the life cycle of a cross-border transaction.</p>
                <p>Our approach combines practical commercial understanding with structured regulatory support so that foreign investments, overseas arrangements and foreign exchange transactions are properly planned and documented.</p>

                <div class="fema-reference-list">
                    <div class="fema-reference-item"><span>01</span><p>Consultation and Compliance for Inbound and Outbound Investments, including transaction structuring and continuing FEMA support.</p></div>
                    <div class="fema-reference-item"><span>02</span><p>Advice and legal opinions under FEMA, applicable rules, regulations, circulars, directions and reporting requirements.</p></div>
                    <div class="fema-reference-item"><span>03</span><p>Annual and regulatory reporting filings relating to foreign investment, overseas investment and prescribed transaction submissions.</p></div>
                    <div class="fema-reference-item"><span>04</span><p>Investment strategy for foreign companies, including suitable routes, ownership structures, permitted activities and regulatory considerations in India.</p></div>
                    <div class="fema-reference-item"><span>05</span><p>Approvals and follow-up under FEMA and FDI frameworks, including preparation, submission and regulatory clarifications.</p></div>
                    <div class="fema-reference-item"><span>06</span><p>Setting up overseas joint ventures and wholly owned subsidiaries for Indian businesses, including structuring, documentation and reporting.</p></div>
                    <div class="fema-reference-item"><span>07</span><p>External Commercial Borrowings, including eligibility evaluation, documentation, reporting and compliance requirements.</p></div>
                    <div class="fema-reference-item"><span>08</span><p>Establishment of branch and representative or liaison offices for foreign business entities, including approvals, registrations and continuing compliance.</p></div>
                    <div class="fema-reference-item"><span>09</span><p>Establishment of joint ventures, associate companies and wholly owned subsidiaries for foreign business entities in India.</p></div>
                    <div class="fema-reference-item"><span>10</span><p>Liaising with Authorised Dealer Banks for foreign exchange transactions, remittances, reporting, documentation and transaction-related clarifications.</p></div>
                </div>
